Shift: Morning /Mid Shifts /evening shifts including weekends &amp; holidays

About the Role

As a Food Safety &amp; Quality Assurance Technician, you will be playing a key role in implementing an effective food safety and quality assurance system.&nbsp; Reporting to the FSQA Supervisor, you will work closely with the Production, Sanitation, and Warehouse teams to uphold our&nbsp; FSQA standards at the plant. This will involve quantitative measurements, environmental and product sampling, inspection of incoming raw materials and observation of the production process.

What you will be doing:

• Complete process monitoring activities and maintain accurate reports and records (ex. GMP records, temp logs);

• Be involved in quality control activities, such as intake, WIP and finished production inspections;

• Perform pre and post-operation and sanitation monitoring of the food processing environment and equipment;

• Perform pre and post-operation and sanitation monitoring of the food processing environment&nbsp;

• Complete record verifications and on-site observations of critical food safety control processes;

• Deliver FSQA training to new and existing associates;

• Conduct pathogen testing sampling and environmental monitoring swabbing/testing;

• Perform equipment calibration verification

• Maintain clear and concise communication with multiple teams including Operations, Procurement, and Sanitation;

• Uphold HelloFresh’s protocol for achieving the highest level of food safety and quality assurance.

• Work in compliance with OH&amp;S acts and regulations.&nbsp;

• Use personal protective and safety equipment and clothing as directed by the employer and report workplace hazards and dangers to the supervisor or employer.

• Other duties as assigned

At a minimum, you have:&nbsp;

• Post-secondary education in Biological, Chemical or Food Sciences or equivalent experience;

• Minimum 1-2 years of experience&nbsp; in a food safety or quality assurance role in the food, cosmetic or other regulated industry.

• Strong understanding of HACCP principles, the Safe Food for Canadians Regulations and GFSI schemes;

• Flexibility to work overtime, weekends, varying shifts and holiday work, as required;

• Willing and able to work in a dynamic environment, which can include warm/humid or cold temperatures;

• Willing and able to push, pull, and lift up to 50lbs

• Ability to prioritize, remain calm and alert while multitasking in a fast-paced and deadline oriented environment;

• Ability to work independently and within a team environment, in addition to having strong interpersonal skills;

• Ability to communicate in English, both verbal and written;

• Strong organizational, analytical, communication and leadership skills;

• Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Google Suite (Calendar, Gmail, Docs, Sheets) and video conferencing (Hangouts, Google Meet);

• Team player who is comfortable collaborating with other departments but also working independently;

• Level 1 First Aid is considered an asset;

What you’ll get in return:

• Competitive salary and health benefits

• Shift premiums are available for afternoon and overnight shifts&nbsp;

• 75% discount on HelloFresh or Chefs Plate weekly box subscription

• High impact work to help feed thousands of families in Canada

• Opportunity to learn and grow

• Work with a hard-working and supportive team

